
=== Reference (Philips_VG_8020) ===
  [ref] arg=12345 ($3039)
    raw snapshot : f6 f7 97 32 9a 00 02 02 00 00 39 30 00 00 00 00
    entering HL  = $F7F6  (arg? no)
    entering DE  = $3297  (arg? no)
    entering BC  = $009A  (arg? no)
    entering A   = $02
    VALTYP       = $02  (hypothesis: 2=integer for ref; 0=unused for zb)
    DAC[0..7]    = 00 00 39 30 00 00 00 00
      DAC+0..1   = $0000  (arg? no)
      DAC+2..3   = $3039  (arg? YES)
  [ref] arg=258 ($0102)
    raw snapshot : f6 f7 97 32 9a 00 02 02 00 00 02 01 00 00 00 00
    entering HL  = $F7F6  (arg? no)
    entering DE  = $3297  (arg? no)
    entering BC  = $009A  (arg? no)
    entering A   = $02
    VALTYP       = $02  (hypothesis: 2=integer for ref; 0=unused for zb)
    DAC[0..7]    = 00 00 02 01 00 00 00 00
      DAC+0..1   = $0000  (arg? no)
      DAC+2..3   = $0102  (arg? YES)

PASS  ref: DAC+2..3 (LE word at offset 2 in DAC) carries the argument value  [12345→DAC+2..3=$3039]
PASS  ref: DAC+0..1 does NOT carry the argument (arg is at DAC+2, not DAC+0)  [12345→DAC+0..1=$0000]
PASS  ref: VALTYP == 2 (integer) when an integer argument is passed  [12345→VALTYP=$02]
PASS  ref: HL == DAC base address $F7F6 on entry (ref leaves HL pointing at DAC)  [12345→HL=$F7F6]
PASS  ref: HL is not the raw argument value (arg is in DAC, not HL itself)  [12345→HL=$F7F6]

