PASS  zb: HL carries the argument value (own-design integer-only convention)  [12345→HL=$3039]
PASS  zb: DAC+2..3 does NOT carry the argument (zerobas skips the DAC/VALTYP protocol)  [12345→DAC+2..3=$0000]
PASS  zb: VALTYP ($F663) not set to 2 by zerobas (DAC/VALTYP protocol not used)  [12345→VALTYP=$00]

=== Measured divergence ===
  reference passes USR arg via DAC+2..3 = LE-word $3039 (= 12345), VALTYP=$02 (integer), HL=$F7F6 (= DAC base address, not the arg itself)
  zerobas  passes USR arg via HL=$3039 (= 12345 = arg), DAC+2..3=$0000 (not the arg), VALTYP=$00 (not set to integer)

  MEASURED DIVERGENCE:
  reference: integer USR argument in DAC+2..3 (LE word); VALTYP=$02
             (integer); HL points to DAC base ($F7F6), not the arg.
  zerobas:   integer USR argument in HL (direct); DAC untouched;
             VALTYP ($F663) not set by zerobas (own-design HL-only
             calling convention, no DAC/VALTYP protocol).

ALL PASS
